      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but if we're being real... isn't the \"preservation\" argument kind of a weak excuse when you consider that the \"global public\" being served is mostly just Western audiences? it feels like the \"universal museum\" concept is just a way to maintain a status quo that benefits former colonial powers. do you think there's actually any valid moral ground for keeping items that were taken under duress, or is that argument fundamentally broken?",
